# ============================================================================
# Orchestrator — what NEVER goes remote.
#
# The tree is ~88% local state by size (code+docs 4.6 MB, state 29.8 MB), so
# this file is the boundary that makes a repo viable at all. Owner's hard rules:
# no evaluation databases stored remotely, no reliance on remote access to work.
#
# Runtime state proper lives OUTSIDE this tree at $ORCH_STATE_DIR (default
# ~/.codex/orchestrator, ~20 GB: the Brain, cadence stamps, worktrees, venvs,
# the capability ledger). That separation is why a second instance needs only a
# different ORCH_STATE_DIR, not a code change.
#
# NOTE ON FORMAT: git does NOT support trailing comments on pattern lines. The
# first version of this file put explanatory comments after each pattern, which
# silently made every pattern inert — 795 files staged instead of 141, including
# the Brain export. Keep comments on their own lines, and verify with
# `git check-ignore -v` or `git status`, never with a hand-rolled parser.
# ============================================================================

# --- evaluation & experiment output: machine-local by the owner's explicit rule ---
# experiments/ is 17 MB / 390 files of per-arm logs, diffs and ship gates.
experiments/
# ux_reviews/ is 2.6 MB / 262 files of UX panel transcripts and scores.
ux_reviews/
# data/ holds feedback-snapshot.json (1.9 MB) — a Brain export, not source.
data/
*.sqlite
*.sqlite3
*.db
# GitHub rate-limit accounting for THIS machine only.
gh-rate-ledger.ndjson

# --- durable audit history belongs to the workspace, not the tool ---
# Code/Audits/Orchestrator/ is the system-of-record for dated decision records;
# capability_admission.commitments() reads it from there. A second copy here
# would be a parallel inventory — the failure mode this project is named for.
Audits/

# --- python / tooling noise ---
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
.venv/
venv/
.pytest_cache/
.mypy_cache/
.ruff_cache/

# --- lock and backup artifacts ---
*.lock
*.bak
*.pre-ingest-fix-*

# --- editor / OS ---
.DS_Store
*.swp

# --- machine-local policy and evidence (the tool is public; the evidence is not) ---
# The split is tool-vs-evidence: generic capabilities and gates ship, while this
# instance's failure history, spend calibration and availability stay local.
# Sanitized public twins of the load-bearing docs are committed under their
# canonical names; these are the full versions.
#
# IMPROVEMENT_BACKLOG.md IS NO LONGER LISTED, ON PURPOSE. Ignoring it made it
# invisible: a gitignored file does not exist in a git worktree, and agents work
# in worktrees, so CLAUDE.md's two mandatory rules about it were unfollowable by
# the workers they bind. The log now lives OUTSIDE the tree at
# $ORCH_LOCAL_RUNTIME, reached via improvement_log.py, and the tracked
# IMPROVEMENT_BACKLOG.md here is a short POINTER to it. Keeping it ignored as
# well would let the 481 KB evidence file reappear at that path silently, which
# is the failure this whole change undoes; tracked, it announces itself in
# `git status` instead. test_improvement_log.py fails if the pointer grows into
# a log.
LOCAL_POLICY.md
CAPABILITY_USEFULNESS.md
*.local.md

# =============================================================================
# Workflows Consumer Repo - Shared Status Files
# =============================================================================
# Auto-generated by workflows; causes merge conflicts if committed.
# Sync from: stranske/Workflows templates/consumer-repo/.gitignore
# Validate: python scripts/sync_status_file_ignores.py --check
# =============================================================================
# Template-Version: 5
# BEGIN WORKFLOWS STATUS FILES

# Agent working files (HIGH conflict risk)
codex-prompt.md
codex-output.md
codex-prompt-*.md
codex-output-*.md
verifier-context.md
verifier-diff-summary.md

# Autofix status files (HIGH conflict risk)
autofix_report_enriched.json
.cosmetic-repair-summary.json
ci/autofix/history.json
ci/autofix/diagnostics.json

# Metrics/history files (MEDIUM conflict risk)
keepalive_status.md
docs/keepalive/status/
keepalive-metrics.ndjson
coverage-trend-history.ndjson
metrics-history.ndjson
metrics-retention.ndjson
residual-trend-history.ndjson
archives/metrics/

# Build artifacts
.autofix-venv/

# PR automation generated files (MEDIUM conflict risk)
pr_body.md

# Local opener/closer lane state (MEDIUM conflict risk)
# Per-repo lane scratch (repo/issue/branch/PR/blocker/next-action) written by
# the local opener/closer lanes; a lane artifact, not a repo deliverable.
# See stranske/Workflows docs/ops/LOCAL_LANES.md.
workloop-state.md

# Test/coverage artifacts
# .coverage is written by every `pytest --cov` run, and coverage is ON in the Gate as of
# 2026-08-23, so it now appears after any local probe too.
.coverage
.coverage.*
coverage.json
coverage.xml

# Wrong package manager artifacts (defense-in-depth)
Pipfile.lock
poetry.lock

# Accidentally-committed dependency trees. The sync script retains the following exceptions
# only when .github/scripts/package.json declares a file:node_modules dependency. Registry-based
# consumers keep the entire tree ignored.
node_modules/
!/.github/scripts/node_modules/
!/.github/scripts/node_modules/**

# END WORKFLOWS STATUS FILES
